## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical cross-account IAM, KMS usage, and end-to-end data flow in a real-world streaming pipeline, plus a concrete test plan.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account trust with IAM roles and principals
- Kinesis PutRecords permissions and TLS enforcement
- SSE-KMS with a CMK in the data-owner account
- Lambda assuming a restricted role using session tags for fine-grained access
- Test strategy: canaries, revocation timing, and anomaly detection

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT_A:role/ProducerRole"},
      "Action": "kinesis:PutRecords",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kinesis:REGION:ACCOUNT_B:stream/STREAM_NAME",
      "Condition": {"Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "true"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake-bucket/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/partner": "Acme"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["kms:Encrypt", "kms:Decrypt", "kms:GenerateDataKey*"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kms:REGION:ACCOUNT_B:key/CMK_ID",
